# Vercel ships the WORKING TREE, not the commit (see CLAUDE.md), so anything
# large sitting in the repo gets uploaded on every deploy whether the web build
# needs it or not. The Android module alone is ~300MB once Gradle has run, and
# uploads were failing part-way on a flaky connection because of it.
#
# Only exclude things the Next.js build in web/ provably cannot need.

# Capacitor app + Gradle build outputs (APKs, intermediates, native .so files)
android-app/

# Medication-catalog source data — already loaded into Postgres
dataset/

# NOT excluded on purpose: src/ and test/ (the Telegram bot and its tests) are
# only a few hundred KB, so excluding them saves nothing measurable while adding
# a real chance of breaking a production build over an import nobody remembered.

# Stale full checkout, excluded from repo-wide greps for the same reason
.claude/
.superpowers/
